## Common Pitfalls and Solutions

### Pitfall 1: Forward References

**Problem**: Rule 300.1 references Rule 401.2 which hasn't been written yet

**Solution**: 
- Document it explicitly: "Note: Rule 401.2 to be defined"
- Write rules in dependency order when possible
- Validator will flag it but allow it if marked intentional

### Pitfall 2: Inconsistent Terminology

**Problem**: Same concept called different things in different rules

**Solution**:
- Documentation Standard catches this
- Pick one term, add others as "See also" in glossary
- Auto-fix updates all documents

### Pitfall 3: Rules That Can't Be Coded

**Problem**: "Players should use their best judgment about..."

**Solution**:
- Rules Validator flags immediately as ERROR
- Redesign rule to be deterministic
- Use explicit conditions instead of judgment

### Pitfall 4: Overly Complex Rules

**Problem**: Rule with depth 6, width 8 (references 8 other rules deeply nested)

**Solution**:
- Validator flags as high complexity
- Break into sub-rules
- Simplify where possible
- Accept complexity if truly necessary (document why)

### Pitfall 5: Missing Edge Cases

**Problem**: Rule works for common case, breaks in edge cases

**Solution**:
- Code Generator creates tests for boundary conditions
- Playtesting reveals edge cases
- Add explicit edge case handling to rule
- Update tests to prevent regression

## Metrics for Success

Track these metrics to ensure the system is working:

**Documentation Quality**:
- % of rules that pass validation on first try
- Average iterations per rule before approval
- Glossary coverage (% of terms defined)
- Cross-reference validity (% of links working)

**Code Quality**:
- Test coverage of generated code
- % of tests passing on first run
- Number of manual edits needed after generation
- Code complexity metrics

**Process Efficiency**:
- Time from rule draft to validated rule
- Time from validated rule to working code
- Number of issues found in playtesting
- Time to fix issues

**Ideal Targets** (after team is experienced with system):
- 80%+ rules pass validation on first try
- 95%+ glossary coverage
- 90%+ tests passing on first run
- Issues found in playtesting are balance, not logic bugs

